# modules_d.tcyr — per-module coverage, fourth part: the 3.5.0 repairs.
# Fifteen blocks, each under its own banner: seven for the areas of the 3.5.0 roadmap (prefix
# _v35L<n>_, L1 to L7), then eight for the rows those left open (prefix _w2W<n>_, W1 to W8), as the
# groups' names and the [measured: ...] markers in src/ name them. The blocks share no name but the
# three tolerances below (the values tests/modules_c.tcyr uses). Each expected value is an exact
# oracle's (Python Fractions or a 120-digit Decimal, correctly rounded) or a closed form's, unless the
# assertion's message says how far it sits. Each block was mutation-tested when it was written.

include "src/f64_util.cyr"
include "src/error.cyr"
