test_group("3.5.0 W3: a tie of support values goes to the closed form, not to rounding (wave-2 review)");
# Two support values within h's rounding (2^-49 of the points' scale) give the depth equally well, and the lower
# is noise; where h is flat their normals can be far apart. The first wave-2 form took the lower at all, in the
# deep snap (_epa_snap_deep), the band (_ga_band_depth) and the rim ring's callers. Now a closed form wins a tie
# and a reading does not (_ga_cf_ties), and a face form that is no minimiser of h is refused (_epa_off_min).
# Exact depths and normals in 120-digit Decimal (eps = 2^-46 M, M a bound on the largest |coordinate|).
# [measured: scratch W3 fix py/pinerr.py and py/chk.py; families C1 to C5 and K1 to K3, py/mutdiff.py; 2026-11-14]
fn _w2W3_nc(k) {
    var n = load64(_w2W3_n);
    if (k == 0) { return HVec3_x(n); }
    if (k == 1) { return HVec3_y(n); }
    return HVec3_z(n);
}
# The review's ball over a cap 8.7e-13 R inside its rim (r 1.66e-6, 210 eps deep, exact 5.6197190971286429e-12,
# the normal the cap's axis): at the near ring's call the rim ring's face form, 0.004 eps above the polished
# depth, is a tie it wins, and in the band again, 0.002 eps above EPA's: 2.0e-16 rad off, 0.0013 eps above the
# exact. The first wave-2 form answered the polish, 1.19e-5 rad off (0x3D98B7265E6A8000). Without the call's tie
# (lower at all), the band's for a closed form (its flag ignored, or taken only where lower) or the near ring's
# flag: EPA's 0x3D98B73800000000, 1.9e-17 rad off.
# [measured: scratch W3 fix probe/fx.txt, py/chk.py (80-digit Decimal), this tree, the merged one, mutants; 2026-11-14]
_w2W3_cyl(0xBFD9858CA664C45C, 0x3F9D338E2243B640, 0x3FEC6C39AD71EB5C, 0xBFE2C84F8E51433E, 0x3FD4005635809C1F,
  0xBFE7E660C538F210, 0x3FDFB027DDDF98CF, 0x3FE57D8F386CB0CD);
_w2W3_ball(0xBFBB7AE1AEAEBEC9, 0x3FCD9D9CC0A64751, 0x3FFA4AC18DD211F6, 0x3EBBE26070E5CA8A);
assert_eq(_w2W3_q(0), 0x3D98B74800000000, "gjk_epa_3d: a ball 17 eps inside a cap's rim: the rim ring's face form");
assert_eq(_w2W3_nc(1), 0xBFD4005635809C22, "gjk_epa_3d: ... its normal 2.0e-16 rad off the axis (y)");
# A ball over a cap 3.7e-13 R inside its rim (r 4.9e-7, 18 eps deep, exact 4.6003620827002702e-13): at the cycling
# proof's call the rim ring's face form replaces EPA's depth, and in the band it is 0.130 eps below EPA's answer,
# a tie it wins: 2.0e-16 rad off, 0.005 eps below the exact. With its flag ignored, or unset at that call, EPA's
# 0x3D604C82639C0000 (3.4.2's): 1.16e-4 rad off, 0.125 eps above.
# [measured: scratch W3 fix probe/fx.txt, py/chk.py (80-digit Decimal), this tree, the merged one, mutants; 2026-11-14]
_w2W3_cyl(0xBFD12BD47A702BE0, 0x3FC2400D6A7903B0, 0x3FEDED27908DA134, 0x3FEB12334F3B32EF, 0x3FD4C5067BC152CE,
  0xBFDB141925519559, 0x3FE424DEAD6EBCE3, 0x3FE1F457A8D627A5);
